          "normalized_title": "Climate Change Is Quietly Choking Rivers Across the Planet",
          "normalized_summary": "Climate change is causing rivers worldwide to lose oxygen, and tropical waterways are being hit hardest. Climate change is causing rivers around the world to lose oxygen at a troubling rate, according to a study published May 15 in Science Advances. Researchers found that this widespread and persistent deoxygenation is affecting river ecosystems globally, with [...]",
